  "explanation": {
    "short": "ö is like e with rounded lips; ü is like i with rounded lips. ch is a soft hiss after e and i (nicht) and a rougher sound from the back of the throat after a, o, u (auch). A vowel followed by h, or doubled, is long: sehr, Tee.",
    "more": "ö and ü have no English match: say e (or i) and then round your lips as for \"oo\". The h after a vowel is not said; it only shows that the vowel is long."
  },
